// Scoped type check.
//
// tsconfig.json has no `include` and sets `allowJs: true`, so tsc sweeps in
// junk at the repo root (fix_ui_13.cjs, scratch/writeb64.js). Those files have
// unterminated string literals, and a syntax error anywhere ABORTS tsc's
// semantic pass — which means `tsc -p tsconfig.json` silently reports nothing
// and `npm run build` (esbuild, transpile-only) never type-checks at all.
//
// The practical consequence: undefined identifiers reach the browser as
// runtime crashes with a green build. This config scopes the check to src/ so
// the semantic pass actually runs.
//
//     npx tsc -p tsconfig.check.json --noEmit
//
// src/ currently carries ~210 pre-existing errors, so a clean run is not the
// bar. Compare against a baseline taken before your change:
//
//     git stash && npx tsc -p tsconfig.check.json --noEmit > base.txt; git stash pop
//     npx tsc -p tsconfig.check.json --noEmit > now.txt
//     diff <(sed 's/([0-9]*,[0-9]*)//' base.txt) <(sed 's/([0-9]*,[0-9]*)//' now.txt)
//
// Stripping (line,col) makes the comparison position-independent, so shifting
// code around does not read as a new error.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx"]
}
